{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think","id":1387902,"title":"Lots of questions (but interesting ones I think)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T21:55:52-07:00","id":1387902,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Lots of questions (but interesting ones I think)","content":"Hello there, it's nice to see we have a dedicated and active Mage community, it is my favorite game from WoD itself, I play the scenario from decades starting with Vampire: The Masquerade and I guess that I play Mage from 5 years, but still the nature of the game leaves me with lots of questions on how some things would run and it's limitations. I've read mostly supplements and loved &quot;How Do You Do That?&quot; but it simply don't kill most of my questions.<br /> So, to prevent flooding the forum and take all the first page at once I'll compile some of my doubts here, don't mind to answer all at once.<br /> <br /> 1 - Time 5 effect from steping out from time flow if I get right you are still there and see the time flowing and events normaly, yet outside phenomenon does't affect you unless you want so (from what I get from the effect), but I got confused about the duration, &quot;HDYDT&quot; says that the effect puts place on a turn-by-turn basis, what does exact that means? You know, straight 1 sucess = 1 turn? If true, how does that takes on non-turn based actions (outside of combat)?<br /> <br /> 2 - Still on Time 5, if for example you got hit by the traffic the car will pass right through you got it, but what does happen if you face a explosion that damage the structure you're on for example? You'll still fall or be throwed away?<br /> <br /> 3 - Time 4 effect ables you to loop situations, based on that, you could put on a damage routine for example to loop the actual effect more than once? I mean for example, you're casting a fireball, you took the 1 sucess to make it ok, and 2 more on damage so it'll do 6 damage, you could add extra sucess on replicating the ball itself to make it do a separate +6 damage for every sucess expended on loop effect?<br /> <br /> 4 - Mind (probably 3), based on a low level Stargazer gift I've thought on a routine to increase the regular automatic sucess you get by spending a point of willpower... BUT THIS SEEMS EXTREMELY EXPLOITABLE, like you could loop rituais to a some point achieve 20, 30, 50 sucesses by a single spending, so would made sense to put as a limitation you could not get more sucesses than your standard Willpower or Arete rating itself?<br /> <br /> 5 - If I want to emulate the KotE power of Ghost-Flame Shintai level 4 Goblin Torch to burn the enemy soul and reap his permanent willpower (after ripping his temporary) that'll be a effect of Forces 3 + Spirit (3?5?) or it'll add Mind to the effect also? Or probably demand mind if you have only spirit 3 probably?<br /> <br /> 6 - Laham merit (BoS), a Laham character will OBLIGATORY be or a evil character or be doomed to become one? You cannot be like some well known half-demon half-human demon hunter? Or maybe take another demon concept from the infinite hells that exists on High Umbra and still have acess to the 7 points investments from the merit to represent your heritage?<br /> <br /> 7 - When building a permanent Wonder you need to spend a Permanent Willpower point as it's on BoS, but there's no further explanation how exactly that behave, I mean, the Willpower is gone for good? It's still on you sheet while you keep the wonder? If the last one is true, you can spend this temporary Willpower? Or you'll eventually get that rating back? If the last one is true you'll have to expend Experience Points for doing so?<br /> <br /> 8 - This is a way more specific, the House Shaea from Order of Hermes has as a &quot;Magic Style&quot; to command to Magick through Enochian Names of the phenomenom, but that doesn't seem to fit very well on the Pratices we got from M20 Sourcebook and BoS, so it'll be a separate pratice like &quot;Words of Power&quot;? Or it'll take place on the High Ritual pratice demanding previous preparation with Language tool? If true you need to use it in a more dinamic and urgent way you'll be on the &quot;working without focus&quot; rule?<br /> <br /> Those last ones it's not a doubt of mine, it's things that I heard on some foruns discussions that just make me &quot;wtf?&quot; but I need some confirmation.<br /> <br /> 9 - If you want to cast a permanent brick, you'll need Matter 5 for doing so or Matter 3 is good for that?<br /> <br /> 10 - A initial sheet Tremere is stronger than a initial sheet Mage? Same level of &quot;combo&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the attention, I'll make a post about paradigm latter, thought on doing here but I think that this questions takes place on a larger and dedicated discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 05-13-2020, 01:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:17:21-07:00","id":1387906,"title":"","content":"I'll answer 7 and 8. <br /> <br /> 7. When you craft a Talisman, Grimoire, Device, or Principia, your Willpower pool shrinks by one until such time as you spend enough Experience on it to raise it back up. In effect, it's an \u201cXP tax\u201d disguised as investing a bit of your Will into the Wonder. <br /> <br /> 8. The Paradigms and Practices are suggestions only. That said, High Ritual Magic frequently includes mystical words of power; in the case of House Shaea, those words are Enochian. Put another way, \u201cwords of power\u201d are an Instrument, not a Practice. <br /> <br /> But if you envision your House Shaea wizard wielding Enochian Words of Power in the same way that DC Comics' Zatanna tosses around her backward-speak and your Storyteller is okay with it, by all means give your mage a Practice that allows Words of Power to be used in that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:26:34-07:00","id":1387909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387906#post1387906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">8. The Paradigms and Practices are suggestions only. That said, High Ritual Magic frequently includes mystical words of power; in the case of House Shaea, those words are Enochian. Put another way, \u201cwords of power\u201d are an Instrument, not a Practice.<br /> <br /> But if you envision your House Shaea wizard wielding Enochian Words of Power in the same way that DC Comics' Zatanna tosses around her backward-speak and your Storyteller is okay with it, by all means give your mage a Practice that allows Words of Power to be used in that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I use &quot;Language&quot; as a Instrument to reflect the description on the Tradition Book like calling &quot;Thunder&quot; and controlling it but the Pratice bound is &quot;High Ritual&quot; it'll demand previous preparation (theatrical and paradigm-wise not roll the spell before) or I'll count as &quot;Work Without Focus&quot;? I'll need to prepare every single effect or idk, a single preparation on the language itself like a few hours a week does the deal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 05-13-2020, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T22:40:59-07:00","id":1387913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think#post1387902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - but I got confused about the duration, &quot;HDYDT&quot; says that the effect puts place on a turn-by-turn basis, what does exact that means? You know, straight 1 sucess = 1 turn? If true, how does that takes on non-turn based actions (outside of combat)?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, this means that time is passing normally for the Mage (and just the mage- see my next answer), and it cannot replace Time Travel spells<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2 - Still on Time 5, if for example you got hit by the traffic the car will pass right through you got it, but what does happen if you face a explosion that damage the structure you're on for example? You'll still fall or be throwed away? </div> </div> </div>You're reading Time 5 Time Immunity wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Time 5 Time Immunity essentially means the entire world around the Mage...stops from their point of view. Unlike with Time 4, where only a certain area or person (see 'Freezing Time') stops.<br /> So, there is no Traffic or explosion to hit the Mage - everything, from their point of view, is not moving at all. Unless they actively decide to interact with it (like opening a door, moving something etc.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3 - Time 4 effect ables you to loop situations, </div> </div> </div>That's time 3.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> based on that, you could put on a damage routine for example to loop the actual effect more than once? </div> </div> </div>Not quite. The Time Loop (see HDYDT Page 111) essentially means that the Mage rewinds time in a small area around them.<br /> The base difference between Time Loop and Reboot (which are very similiar) is, that in the case of the Time Loop, the Mage remains how and where they are while the rest of the area turns back, and in the case of the Reboot, the Mage itself also turns back (including positioning, any wounds etc.), but still remembers everything that happened.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4 - Mind (probably 3), based on a low level Stargazer gift I've thought on a routine to increase the regular automatic sucess you get by spending a point of willpower... BUT THIS SEEMS EXTREMELY EXPLOITABLE </div> </div> </div>I am not sure how you would increase the successes you get from spending WP with Mind 3/4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5 - If I want to emulate the KotE power of Ghost-Flame Shintai level 4 Goblin Torch to burn the enemy soul and reap his permanent willpower (after ripping his temporary) that'll be a effect of Forces 3 + Spirit (3?5?) or it'll add Mind to the effect also? </div> </div> </div>Forces would not be involved, as this does not seem to involve a literal fire, but more a..metaphysical fire. Personally I would make this a pure Mind 4 effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6 - Laham merit (BoS), a Laham character will OBLIGATORY be or a evil character or be doomed to become one? </div> </div> </div>I don't think so, no. But the Laham would probably attract the attention of demonic entities and spirits that surely would like that to happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Could make for a dramatic character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 7 - When building a permanent Wonder you need to spend a Permanent Willpower point as it's on BoS </div> </div> </div>As Dataweaver said, you only need to spend a permanent Willpower for Talismans and Grimoires and Principae - because Talismans have their own Arete separate from the Mage's Arete pool, the Mage needs to invest a part of themselves into it, and Grimoires also require this kind of personal investment.<br /> Note that the Technocracy has perfected the creation of the Talisman/Device of Wonder in such a way that they do not need to invest that Permanent Willpower - *if* the Wonder is being created at a specialied Technocratic Facility (i.e. probably in no way owned by a player character)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 10 - A initial sheet Tremere is stronger than a initial sheet Mage? Same level of &quot;combo&quot;. </div> </div> </div>This is hard to answer, because this is so-called White-Room territory. What are the stats of the Tremere? What are the stats and spheres of the Mage? Note that such discussions uuuusually end up with weird super-specialized-to-beat-that-other-sheet characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-13-2020, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:03:17-07:00","id":1387918,"title":"","content":"\u201cWork Without Focus\u201d is a bit more extreme than you need. Look at \u201cfast-casting in a fight\u201d, M20 p.415.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:26:08-07:00","id":1387928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're reading Time 5 Time Immunity wrong <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Time 5 Time Immunity essentially means the entire world around the Mage...stops from their point of view. Unlike with Time 4, where only a certain area or person (see 'Freezing Time') stops.<br /> So, there is no Traffic or explosion to hit the Mage - everything, from their point of view, is not moving at all. Unless they actively decide to interact with it (like opening a door, moving something etc.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh okay I got it, but there's some way to sidestep the timeline and still let the events occurs normally as described using another spheres together?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's time 3.<br /> Not quite. The Time Loop (see HDYDT Page 111) essentially means that the Mage rewinds time in a small area around them.<br /> The base difference between Time Loop and Reboot (which are very similiar) is, that in the case of the Time Loop, the Mage remains how and where they are while the rest of the area turns back, and in the case of the Reboot, the Mage itself also turns back (including positioning, any wounds etc.), but still remembers everything that happened.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmn, got it, but with the level 4 you could make some event occuring over and over and over right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure how you would increase the successes you get from spending WP with Mind 3/4.</div> </div> </div> </div>This one I get the inspiration from this gift:<br /> <br /> &quot;Iron Resolve<br /> Rank 1 Stargazer Gift<br /> <br /> Through the blessings of the spirits, the Stargazer\u2019s resolve is tempered like steel, allowing great feats through application of sheer will. An ancestor-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <br /> System: Once per scene, the Stargazer may spend one Willpower to gain two automatic successes on an action, rather than one.<br /> <br /> Source: 20th Anniversary Edition&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces would not be involved, as this does not seem to involve a literal fire, but more a..metaphysical fire. Personally I would make this a pure Mind 4 effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>My question about the it's because the foundament of Goblin-Torch itself burns the target soul (sorry I didn't made me very clear on this one), so I thought that Spirit would be somewhat envolved with the WP lost reflecting the &quot;soulburn&quot;. So I don't know if the &quot;A Little Bit of Spirit?&quot; rule would apply to a mind effect to reflect it or Spirit would be the primary sphere of the route itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think so, no. But the Laham would probably attract the attention of demonic entities and spirits that surely would like that to happen <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Could make for a dramatic character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure it does, would be cool taking the Spirit Magnet Flaw to reflect evil spirits trying to corrupt the character or even as a Merit (why not both?) to reflect good spirits trying to save the character too.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387913#post1387913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is hard to answer, because this is so-called White-Room territory. What are the stats of the Tremere? What are the stats and spheres of the Mage? Note that such discussions uuuusually end up with weird super-specialized-to-beat-that-other-sheet characters <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> I got myself on this discussion a few days ago, and somewhat the dude categorically stated that the Tremere we're stronger and they just become vampires because vampires are indeed stronger and lost nothing. And in most situations the Tremere will ALWAYS have the advantage, needing ARCHMASTERY for a Mage to match a neophyte. This, literally, he stated that you need Matter 5 in order to make a permanent brick or Prime 4 to make it a Wonder so it lasts...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1387902-lots-of-questions-but-interesting-ones-i-think?p=1387918#post1387918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u201cWork Without Focus\u201d is a bit more extreme than you need. Look at \u201cfast-casting in a fight\u201d, M20 p.415.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26165,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","user":"GothicxXx","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26165-gothicxxx","name":"GothicxXx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26165_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T06:35:43-07:00","id":1388016,"title":"","content":"It is mentioned more than once in the M20 line that Matter 5 will make changes permanent, however even Matter 3 can make the duration permanent with enough successes so the argument is kinda mute. Though the Matter 3 permanent effect could be dispelled with countermagic.<br /> <br /> As far as this &quot;dude's&quot; Tremere claims this is just what Ambrosia is talking about. All these claims become pissing matches of which really have no merit to them. I can make X to beat your Y but someone else's Z could defeat that. Yippy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 05-13-2020, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:34:36-07:00","id":1388086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GothicxXx</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This one I get the inspiration from this gift:<br /> <br /> &quot;Iron Resolve<br /> Rank 1 Stargazer Gift<br /> <br /> Through the blessings of the spirits, the Stargazer\u2019s resolve is tempered like steel, allowing great feats through application of sheer will. An ancestor-spirit teaches this Gift.<br /> <br /> System: Once per scene, the Stargazer may spend one Willpower to gain two automatic successes on an action, rather than one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any manipulation of Willpower with Magick it's going to require a level of fiat/houserule on your STs part. It's not an aspect of the system that's well integrated into the magick system. There's nothing in the core rules explicitly pointing out that Willpower *can* be affected by magick (and I don't quite remember any Rote that does it rigth now)<br /> <br /> That being said, mage encourages STs to invent ways for every element to interact with the magick system (as magick supposedly can do everything). For instance, in my table Mind 3 allows the mage to &quot;channel&quot; more than one point of Willpower per turn. You should talk with your ST about shifting/manipulating WP with magick. Maybe the Gift itself can't be copied, but there could be other ways of getting more bang of that Trait<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My question about the it's because the foundament of Goblin-Torch itself burns the target soul (sorry I didn't made me very clear on this one), so I thought that Spirit would be somewhat envolved with the WP lost reflecting the &quot;soulburn&quot;. So I don't know if the &quot;A Little Bit of Spirit?&quot; rule would apply to a mind effect to reflect it or Spirit would be the primary sphere of the route itself. </div> </div> </div>I do not like that rule, but here we enter on *another* aspect of the system that's not well developed and would require your STs fiat:<br /> <br /> Goblin-Torch spirit-fire in it's own game seems to be something that...well...exists.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really have a definition in Mage, though. Hence to summon it (and the same with honest-to-good Abyss Obtenebration, and any other esoterical element from other games) you need your ST to define WHAT *IS* this spirit-flame in Mage terms. It may as well be Mind (Mind it's not just toughts, it also touches aspects of the Umbra). It may also be Spirit + Forces, like how hellfire it's represented in the Cruzade book about Infernalism. It depends on your ST<br /> <br /> And about Lahams:<br /> It's a neat moment to remember that Merlin was a half-demon himself. Only for that I already like that Merit. And yeah, they can be good but are liable to be tempted, as was said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-13-2020, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}